8394	{"artifactId":"LLD-1485159578d9c257-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-1485159578d9c257-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-16T07:02:27.149Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers both sides the request names (implement prompts and the design.story alternatives step) and the source credit, without building the rejected steering-block alternative","evidence":"Section 3 call sites cover scope-prompts.ts, implement-task.md, render.ts (both implement renderers) and design-story/index.ts alternatives.enumerate; a3 (steering-block.md) is rejected and steering is listed as unchanged. The design says plainly that ac1-ac5 were derived because the Story has none, so there is no upstream criterion it could have missed. [files: src/workflow/runners/design-story/index.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/render.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The implement template already fills a mergeRule placeholder in renderImplementPrompt, and the new smallestChangeRule placeholder can be filled the same way","evidence":"render.ts:167 `fill(template, { ...baseVars(repoPath, ref), resolvedDecisions: decisions, mergeRule: MERGE_RULE })`; implement-task.md:34 `{{mergeRule}}`. fill() (render.ts:80-83) leaves unknown keys as literal `{{key}}`, so an unfilled placeholder would show up as literal braces, as the error path says. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/render.ts, src/prompts/build/implement-task.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"renderStandaloneImplementPrompt is built inline, has a Definition of done, a Small-only Submitting the tests section and a Merging upstream section, and the Trivial branch says 'smallest correct edit'","evidence":"render.ts:198-230: lines array with '## Definition of done', STANDALONE_MAPPING_RULE under '## Submitting the tests' when lldMdRel is set, '## Merging upstream' MERGE_RULE; line 210 'make the smallest correct edit that satisfies the scope'. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/render.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The alternatives.enumerate prompt has a HARD RULES list ending in ANTI_OVERREACH_RULE, which the new rule can join","evidence":"design-story/index.ts:200-204: 'HARD RULES:' followed by three bullets and then ANTI_OVERREACH_RULE. [files: src/workflow/runners/design-story/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"SMALLEST_CHANGE_RULE, SMALLEST_SHAPE_RULE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md do not exist yet; scope-prompts.ts is the existing home of the shared fragment ANTI_OVERREACH_RULE","evidence":"A grep for 'smallest' finds no such constants (only unrelated test helpers and render.ts:210). scope-prompts.ts exports only ANTI_OVERREACH_RULE. A glob finds LICENSE at the root but no THIRD_PARTY*. [files: src/workflow/runners/scope-prompts.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"render.ts (daemon) can import a constant from src/workflow/runners/scope-prompts.ts without a new layering dependency","evidence":"render.ts:20-22 already imports from '../../../workflow/storage.js', '../../../workflow/tracker/resolve.js' and '../../../workflow/artifacts/plan.js'. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/render.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every implement prompt site is listed: renderImplementPrompt (template) and renderStandaloneImplementPrompt (Small and Trivial); the validate prompts are left alone","evidence":"render.ts defines renderImplementPrompt (162) and renderStandaloneImplementPrompt (198) as the implement renderers; renderValidatePrompt and renderStandaloneValidatePrompt are the judge prompts and are rightly left out. The call-site list covers both renderer files and the template. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/render.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing 'adjacent-scope' source-reading test pattern can be extended to check that each site references the shared constants without breaking its current count assertion","evidence":"adjacent-scope-gate.test.ts:148-159 reads design-story/index.ts and plan/index.ts and asserts ANTI_OVERREACH_RULE refs >= 6. Adding SMALLEST_SHAPE_RULE does not lower that count. The same readFileSync approach can cover render.ts. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/adjacent-scope-gate.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The change is additive prompt text only, with no stored shape, schema, IPC or artifact format change","evidence":"The touched surfaces are string constants, a markdown template and inline prompt lines. The alternatives step's schema is unchanged and no persisted type is touched (render.ts and design-story/index.ts were read). No migration of older records is needed. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/render.ts, src/workflow/runners/design-story/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An unfilled {{smallestChangeRule}} placeholder can be detected by a test that renders the prompt and checks for leftover braces, as is already done for mergeRule","evidence":"render.test.ts:102 `assert.equal(prompt.includes('{{mergeRule}}'), false, 'the placeholder is filled')`. fill() leaves unknown keys literal (render.ts:81-83), so the check catches a missing fill. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/__tests__/render.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/render.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The notice's stated facts (Ponytail is MIT-licensed, copyright 2026 DietrichGebert, at github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail) are correct","evidence":"These are facts about an external repository. Nothing in this repo or its docs records them, and I did not fetch the upstream LICENSE. The design cites only an analyze bundle (c4) for them.","action":"The builder should copy the copyright line and licence text verbatim from the upstream LICENSE when writing THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each derived criterion ac1-ac5 maps to a test, and the fixtures the tests reuse (TASK, the standalone Small and Trivial specs) exist in render.test.ts","evidence":"The acceptance mapping maps ac1-ac5 to named subjects. render.test.ts:24-39 defines the TASK fixture, and lines 92-96 already render the plan-driven, standalone Small and standalone Trivial implement prompts together, so the 'every implement prompt' subject can extend that loop. [files: src/daemon/steps/build-step/__tests__/render.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":12,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-16T07:02:27.149Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
